s in the 2011  event series fear itself upon Thor's  apparent death Steve Rogers lifts the  hammer once again to rally the Avengers  and probably the most controversial  instance the Hydra allegiant version of  Captain America raises the hammer and  2017 s secret Empire the moment is also  a callback to Avengers age of Ultron  where Steve tries to lift me ol near but  it doesn't quite pull it off  a lot of MCU superheroes have daughters  that appear in endgame and almost all of  them are direct or indirect versions of  characters from comics the most direct  comics connection is Cassie Lange who  appears in endgame as a teenager in the  comics she's a teenaged sighs changing  superhero who goes by the name of  stature and joins the Young Avengers  Scott even remarks to her in the movie  you're so big I ain't fair for breakfast  super cool in end games opening moments  we see clint barton training a young  girl who we find out is his daughter  lilah in archery a quick glimpse of that  scene in the trailer had some observers  thinking the girl might be Kate bishop  who also goes by hawkeye in the comics  it isn't but as sure not decayed occurs  when Clint calls Lila Hawkeye then  there's Morgan stark Tony's daughter who  loves him 3,000 in the comics however  Morgan Stark is a very different  character he's Tony's cousin and  believes Tony's dad stole all his ideas  from his father he teams up with  supervillain count nefaria to try to  kill Tony and later turns into a giant  living robot  he doesn't love Tony 3000 a lingering  question from Avengers infinity war was  whether any of the Asgardians who were  in the ship Thanos attacked survived to  resettle on earth as they plan to do at  the end of thor ragnarok buddhism  endgame lets us know that they did  building a small but thriving new Asgard  community headed up by Valkyrie in  Thor's absence though there's never been  a comics version of Asgard in the Nordic  region there have been a couple times  Asgard came to earth the version  actually called new Asgard is from a  story where an alternate future Thor has  become Lord of both earth and Asgard in  the year 2020 and Asgard has been  rebuilt over the remains of a devastated  New York City once all that got reversed  Thor eventually created a version of  Asgard on a giant landmass hovering  nearby the town of Broxton Oklahoma for  a while many of the hair and costume  choices and endgame either point to the  passage of time like black widows blonde  red to tone hair mix or dig into the  history of the MCU Captain America wears  almost every previous movie costume to  character looks are definite nods to  comic fans though the red and blue  ensemble Rocket wears is a version of  the red and blue out  rocket in the rest of the guardians of  the galaxy team war after the mid-2000s  annihilation event  there's also captain Marvel's new  haircut which rocket cracks a joke about  just after the five-year jump it's very  similar to the hairstyle Carol Danvers  currently sports in the comics and which  she's had since taking up the Captain  Marvel name in 2012 Gwyneth Paltrow's  Pepper Potts wears one of Tony's suits  in Iron Man 3 and later gets superpowers  by the end of the movie but she hadn't  had a flying armored suit all her own  until the final act of Avengers endgame  who's the hot mess now still debatable  though she isn't called by the name in  the movie this is undoubtedly the MCS  version of rescue the armored identity  comics pepper took up in 2009's  invincible Iron Man number 10 in that  story Tony goes underground having been  publicly shamed for a recent squirrel  invasion pepper is tasked with running  Stark Industries responsibly upon  unleashing her fury at Tony by throwing  a chair at the wall she opens up a  secret room with the rescue armor inside  and begins her super heroic career in  the movie Tony makes the armor for her  willingly no chair throwing required the  Hulk's absence and the trailers for  end